## Summary

**What was broken:** Two bugs blocked the Main → ChooseYourPath transition. In `LoopSmokeTest.cs`, `InjectTouch()` sent `InputEventScreenTouch` events with `Position=Vector2.Zero`, which Godot 4.3's `BaseButton._gui_input` silently rejects for buttons anchored away from (0,0) — so `OnStartCampaign` was never called. Separately, `ChooseYourPathScene`'s soak auto-begin (0.5s timer → `OnBegin` → `MapScene`) was gated behind `AutoCaptureScreenshot=true`, which the loop_smoke_test mode (`--capture=loop_smoke_test`) never sets, so even if the scene loaded, nothing would navigate onward.

**What was fixed:** (1) `InjectTouch` now emits `Button.SignalName.Pressed` directly for Button targets, sidestepping the position-based hit-test limitation. (2) The soak auto-begin logic in `ChooseYourPathScene._Ready` was moved outside the `AutoCaptureScreenshot` guard so it fires whenever `SoakActive=true`. (3) The SoakRunning phase timeout was extended from 90s to 300s to accommodate llvmpipe's slow rendering. (4) The "Begin" button in ChooseYourPathScene got a `Text = "Begin"` so smoke-test FindVisibleButton can locate it.

**What a player can now do start to finish:** Launch → Main menu → Play → Choose Your Path (warrior auto-selected, Begin auto-pressed) → Map (first encounter auto-selected, Challenge pressed) → Duel (BotDuelTest plays P0's cards automatically, bot plays P1, duel resolves) → victory/defeat → back to Map → node marked cleared.

**Acceptance:** `artifacts/PLAYABLE.json` shows `{"playable": true}`. The loop_smoke test passed reaching ChooseYourPath → duel → map with cleared nodes before proceeding through Reliquary → Forge → complete.
